const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What are the main preconstruction priorities for an apartment community?",
    answer: "Useful early priorities include validating scope and assumptions, coordinating unit types and finish standards, reviewing site and utility constraints, planning building starts, identifying long-lead decisions, mapping permit and inspection requirements, and aligning the budget and schedule with the owner's intended turnover sequence.",
  },
  {
    question: "How are amenities and resident-facing spaces coordinated?",
    answer: "Leasing areas, clubhouses, fitness rooms, pools, landscape, parking, and other shared spaces should be included in the procurement, quality, inspection, and turnover plan—not treated as separate last-minute work. The agreement and project documents establish which spaces and responsibilities are included.",
  },
  {
    question: "What goes into unit punch and building turnover?",
    answer: "Turnover planning may include unit and common-area inspections, correction tracking, required testing, authority approvals, owner reviews, training, record information, keys and access items, and other closeout deliverables. Requirements vary by jurisdiction, contract, building, and intended occupancy milestone.",
